<p><m>\displaystyle{b}=</m> <fillin characters="7"/>
  </p>
<p>Round to 2 decimal places.</p>


</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>210.33</li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p>We want to know the length of a side opposite a known angle. The law of sines could help. However, we do not yet know the angle across from the known side.</p>
<p>We calculate that using the known measures of the other two angles. <m>\displaystyle{180}^{\circ}-{82}^{\circ}-{52}^{\circ}={46}^{\circ}</m>.</p>
<p>Now we can use law of sines to calculate the desired side length.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle\frac{{\sin{{\left({52}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{b}}=\frac{{\sin{{\left({46}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{192}}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{192}{\sin{{\left({52}^{\circ}\right)}}}={b}{\sin{{\left({46}^{\circ}\right)}}}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{192}\frac{{\sin{{\left({52}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{\sin{{\left({46}^{\circ}\right)}}}}={b}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{210.32906092679}={b}</m></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{210.33}\approx{b}</m></p>
  </solution>
